4.95}],"validation_categories":[{"id":"official_examples","title":"Official worked examples","what":"The engine reproduces Tesouro Nacional's and Tesouro Direto's published worked examples exactly (LTN, NTN-F, LFT, NTN-B, Renda+ and Educa+), including all 300 published business-day counts.","independence":"Fully independent: expected values are transcribed from official documents and frozen in tests/fixtures."},{"id":"nominal_history","title":"Fixed-rate history (independent prediction)","what":"Every historical Tesouro Prefixado (LTN) and Prefixado-with-coupons (NTN-F) price is recomputed from the published rate alone.","independence":"Independent: no input is taken from the price being checked; only the published rate and the calendar are used."},{"id":"implied_vna","title":"IPCA-linked history (cross-sectional consistency)","what":"For IPCA-linked bonds, Tesouro does not publish its daily projected VNA. On each date the VNA is inferred from that day's official prices and the test checks whether one VNA reproduces every IPCA-linked price to the cent.","independence":"Not independent prediction: the VNA is fitted from the same prices. It verifies that the cash-flow and rounding engine is consistent across very different bond structures."},{"id":"independent_vna","title":"Independent VNA reconstruction","what":"A VNA built only from IBGE IPCA index numbers (or BCB Selic rates) is compared with the price-implied VNA.","independence":"Independent inputs, but the IPCA projection for the current month uses the realised IPCA instead of the ANBIMA projection Tesouro uses, so differences of a few basis points are expected."},{"id":"limitations","title":"Known discrepancies and limits","what":"Tesouro Selic spreads are published with 2 decimals, which limits cent-level reconciliation after 2020; residual mismatches concentrate on a few dates and securities close to maturity; Tesouro IGPM+ has no second security for a VNA cross-check.","independence":"Documented, not correct